{"task": "Prove exactly this local conditional obligation using the supplied NL route. Return only the tactic body through submit_transition. All displayed parameter and input proof binders are already in context.", "packet": {"version": 2, "contract_sha256": "b899a2e0303ad3cf09f48c7a036fe5e600316bb0c158bc8f3498f0372a6cd0ed", "header": "import Mathlib
open MeasureTheory Set Filter
open scoped BigOperators ContDiff
noncomputable section
namespace WaveMap
abbrev Space (d : ℕ) := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)
def positive (n : ℕ) : Set (Space n × ℝ) := {p | 0 < p.2}
def box (n : ℕ) (R : ℝ) : Set (Space n) := {x | ∀ j, x j ∈ Icc (-R) R}
def openBox (n : ℕ) (R : ℝ) : Set (Space n) := {x | ∀ j, x j ∈ Ioo (-R) R}
def timeInterval (t : ℝ) : Set ℝ := Icc (t / 2) (3 * t / 2)
def timeInterior (t : ℝ) : Set ℝ := Ioo (t / 2) (3 * t / 2)
def spatial {n : ℕ} {F : Type} [NormedAddCommGroup F] [NormedSpace ℝ F]
    (f : Space n → F) (j : Fin n) (x : Space n) : F :=
  fderiv ℝ f x (PiLp.single 2 j 1)
def ut {n m : ℕ} (u : Space n × ℝ → Space m) (x : Space n) (t : ℝ) : Space m :=
  deriv (fun r => u (x, r)) t
def utt {n m : ℕ} (u : Space n × ℝ → Space m) (x : Space n) (t : ℝ) : Space m :=
  deriv (ut u x) t
def ux {n m : ℕ} (u : Space n × ℝ → Space m) (j : Fin n) (x : Space n) (t : ℝ) : Space m :=
  spatial (fun y => u (y, t)) j x
def uxx {n m : ℕ} (u : Space n × ℝ → Space m) (j : Fin n) (x : Space n) (t : ℝ) : Space m :=
  spatial (fun y => ux u j y t) j x
def utx {n m : ℕ} (u : Space n × ℝ → Space m) (j : Fin n) (x : Space n) (t : ℝ) : Space m :=
  spatial (fun y => ut u y t) j x
def laplace {n m : ℕ} (u : Space n × ℝ → Space m) (x : Space n) (t : ℝ) : Space m :=
  ∑ j, uxx u j x t
def density {n m : ℕ} (u : Space n × ℝ → Space m) (x : Space n) (t : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  ‖ut u x t‖ ^ 2 + ∑ j, ‖ux u j x t‖ ^ 2
def densityTime {n m : ℕ} (u : Space n × ℝ → Space m) (x : Space n) (t : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  deriv (density u x) t
def energy {n m : ℕ} (u : Space n × ℝ → Space m) (t : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  ∫ x, density u x t
def kineticProduct {n m : ℕ} (u : Space n × ℝ → Space m) (t : ℝ) (x : Space n) : ℝ :=
  inner ℝ (ut u x t) (utt u x t)
def gradientProduct {n m : ℕ} (u : Space n × ℝ → Space m) (j : Fin n) (t : ℝ) (x : Space n) : ℝ :=
  inner ℝ (ux u j x t) (utx u j x t)
def laplaceProduct {n m : ℕ} (u : Space n × ℝ → Space m) (j : Fin n) (t : ℝ) (x : Space n) : ℝ :=
  inner ℝ (ut u x t) (uxx u j x t)
def flux {n m : ℕ} (u : Space n × ℝ → Space m) (j : Fin n) (t : ℝ) (x : Space n) : ℝ :=
  inner ℝ (ut u x t) (ux u j x t)
def terms {n m : ℕ} (u : Space n × ℝ → Space m) (t : ℝ) (j : Fin n) : List (Space n → ℝ) :=
  [fun x => density u x t, fun x => densityTime u x t, kineticProduct u t,
   gradientProduct u j t, laplaceProduct u j t, flux u j t, spatial (flux u j t) j]
def quotient {n m : ℕ} (u : Space n × ℝ → Space m) (t h : ℝ) (x : Space n) : ℝ :=
  (density u x (t + h) - density u x t) / h
def bound (n : ℕ) (R B : ℝ) : Space n → ℝ :=
  (box n R).indicator (fun _ => B)
end WaveMap
", "parameters": [{"name": "n", "type": "ℕ"}, {"name": "m", "type": "ℕ"}, {"name": "u", "type": "WaveMap.Space n × ℝ → WaveMap.Space m"}, {"name": "q", "type": "WaveMap.Space m"}], "representation": "Use one ambient Euclidean representation throughout: Space d = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d) = PiLp 2 (fun _ => ℝ). Its norm and real inner product are the Euclidean ones; PiLp.inner_apply identifies the latter with the coordinate dot product. Fin n labels the original n coordinates by j.val + 1; it introduces neither a missing endpoint nor an extra coordinate. PiLp.single 2 j 1 is the unit vector in coordinate j, so spatial is the Fréchet derivative evaluated on that vector. ut and utt are successive ordinary time derivatives, uxx successive same-coordinate spatial derivatives, and utx is the spatial derivative of ut. Under H002 equality of mixed derivatives identifies utx with the time derivative of ux; proving this identification is part of T004/T007, not a hidden assumption. densityTime is the ACTUAL time derivative of the density, not an assumed product formula. The parameter u is an arbitrary total ambient representative; H002 and all geometric hypotheses concern only positive times. Any source map extends by zero for t≤0, without requiring boundary regularity, and restriction recovers it. Since positive times form an open set, derivatives of all orders and energy germs there depend only on that restriction. No conclusion concerns the chosen exterior values. ContDiffOn uses (∞ : ℕ∞ω), meaning every finite derivative order, not ω (analyticity) or the top element of ℕ∞ω. Header definitions assert no regularity or integrability. The total Bochner integral in energy gains its intended finite Lebesgue meaning only after T003 proves integrability. volume is standard normalized Euclidean Lebesgue measure; EuclideanSpace.volume_preserving_symm_measurableEquiv_toLp identifies it with product coordinate Lebesgue measure. In N002, iteratedFDeriv of positive natural order is the multilinear encoding of all mixed space/time derivatives: evaluation on coordinate unit vectors recovers them, and multilinearity plus the coordinate basis gives the converse. All this is in the same Euclidean representation; local product-coordinate measure transport in T008 is checked inside that obligation. No M ports are retained: the four supplied library theorems are used directly under their actual hypotheses. H003 is preserved although the source proof never needs the norm of q. For measures, ENNReal.ofReal ((2*R)^n) encodes a nonnegative real box volume; R>0 and the explicit non-top clause prevent treating an infinite mass as a real finite integral. Integrable means almost everywhere strong measurability together with finite integral of the norm. The supplied dominated-convergence theorem requires these norm and measurability conditions, not merely pointwise convergence. For the scalar FTC, ℝ supplies completeness; the derivative must exist on the unordered closed interval and its function must be interval integrable. Fubini will be used with finite restricted coordinate measures, hence s-finite, and a genuinely integrable real function. These typeclass capabilities are properties of the chosen standard spaces and measures, not additional hypotheses on the wave map.", "inputs": [{"id": "H002", "binder": "h_H002", "type": "ContDiffOn ℝ (∞ : ℕ∞ω) u (WaveMap.positive n)"}, {"id": "H004", "binder": "h_H004", "type": "∀ (x : WaveMap.Space n) (t : ℝ), 0 < t → ‖u (x,t)‖ = 1"}, {"id": "H005", "binder": "h_H005", "type": "∀ (x : WaveMap.Space n) (t : ℝ), 0 < t → ∃ a : ℝ, WaveMap.utt u x t - WaveMap.laplace u x t = a • u (x,t)"}], "target": "∀ (x : WaveMap.Space n) (t : ℝ), 0 < t →
  inner ℝ (u (x,t)) (WaveMap.ut u x t) = 0 ∧
  inner ℝ (WaveMap.ut u x t) (WaveMap.utt u x t - WaveMap.laplace u x t) = 0 ∧
  inner ℝ (u (x,t)) (WaveMap.utt u x t) = -(‖WaveMap.ut u x t‖ ^ 2) ∧
  (∀ j : Fin n, inner ℝ (u (x,t)) (WaveMap.uxx u j x t) = -(‖WaveMap.ux u j x t‖ ^ 2)) ∧
  (∀ a : ℝ, WaveMap.utt u x t - WaveMap.laplace u x t = a • u (x,t) →
    a = (∑ j, ‖WaveMap.ux u j x t‖ ^ 2) - ‖WaveMap.ut u x t‖ ^ 2) ∧
  WaveMap.utt u x t - WaveMap.laplace u x t =
    ((∑ j, ‖WaveMap.ux u j x t‖ ^ 2) - ‖WaveMap.ut u x t‖ ^ 2) • u (x,t)", "explanation": "Full N001. Differentiate the unit constraint once and twice in time and in each coordinate on the positive-time open set; dot normality with u and ut. Choose a only pointwise and prove its value for every scalar satisfying normality; never differentiate a.", "source_steps": [{"id": "S001", "text": "Fix arbitrary x∈ℝ^n and a real t, temporarily assuming L1: t>0. By H002 the component functions are smooth near (x,t). H004 gives u·u=1 in that neighborhood. Differentiating this identity in time by the componentwise product rule gives 2u·u_t=0, hence u·u_t=0. All quantities in this paragraph are evaluated at (x,t)."}, {"id": "S002", "text": "H005 at (x,t) provides a real a with u_tt−Delta u=a u; choose one. By F001 and symmetry of the inner product, u_t·(u_tt−Delta u)=a(u_t·u)=0. No derivative of a has been taken."}, {"id": "S003", "text": "The same twice-differentiated unit constraint gives 0=∂_t²(u·u)=2|u_t|²+2u·u_tt, so u·u_tt=−|u_t|². For each spatial coordinate j from 1 through n, differentiating twice in that coordinate gives 0=2|∂_{x_j}u|²+2u·∂_{x_jx_j}u, so u·∂_{x_jx_j}u=−|∂_{x_j}u|². Dotting the chosen normality equation with u and using u·u=1 yields a=u·u_tt−Σ_j u·∂_{x_jx_j}u=Σ_j|∂_{x_j}u|²−|u_t|². This calculation uses only the equation for a, and therefore holds for every real scalar satisfying that equation at this point. Substitution gives u_tt−Delta u=(Σ_j|∂_{x_j}u|²−|u_t|²)u. Combine this with F001 and F002, discharge L1 to retain t>0 as the quantifier condition, and universally quantify x and t. This proves all the asserted pointwise identities and the explicit equation."}], "boundary": "Only listed inputs are project premises. The pinned Mathlib environment is freely available; no sibling proof is supplied.", "background_supplement_sha256": "227c935068aa7190a4378d88365ed43b5aef18c9f514dc9ed3d66e20d77f91ae", "objects": [], "representations": [], "bridges": [], "shared_inputs": [], "background_note_index": [{"id": "R001.BG001", "at": "/inference/argument/0/text", "kind": "mathematical", "fact": "For a smooth map v from an open subset of ℝ^n×ℝ to ℝ^m, the derivative in any available time or spatial coordinate s satisfies ∂_s(v·v)=2v·∂_s v. If v·v=1 in a neighborhood, this derivative is zero there."}, {"id": "R001.BG002", "at": "/inference/argument/2/text", "kind": "mathematical", "fact": "For a C² Euclidean-valued map v near a point and a time or spatial coordinate s, ∂_s²(v·v)=2|∂_s v|²+2v·∂_s²v. Consequently a locally unit-length v satisfies v·∂_s²v=−|∂_s v|²."}]}}
